  "analysis": {
    "overall_status": "partial_outage",
    "severity": "major",
    "suspected_causes": [
      "All 4 major ISP international gateways (TIC x2, Irancell, Asiatech) remain externally unreachable while BGP routes hold — sustained stealth blackout posture with centralized DPI + protocol whitelist at national gateway layer, consistent with Bock et al. FOCI'20 whitelister architecture",
      "Gateway failure-mode taxonomy shows dynamic instability: Irancell GW (5.232.0.1) reverted from TCP RST ('connection refused') back to silent i/o timeout — this oscillation (timeout → RST → timeout) across three observation passes suggests active DPI appliance reconfiguration or firmware tuning, not a stable policy state",
      "Protocol whitelist enforcement stable at 4.3% — 46 of 1,068 labeled IP ranges reachable across 78 operators (up 1 from 45, within noise margin); UDP/ICMP/SSH/VPN silently dropped at gateway per IRBlock (Tai et al.) USENIX Security '25",
      "Electro DNS (78.157.42.100) persistently timing out while Shecan (178.22.122.100, 223ms) and TIC DNS (217.218.155.155, 229ms) remain operational — sustained targeted suppression of anti-censorship DNS resolver infrastructure",
      "Asiatech dual failure persists — gateway (94.182.0.1 timeout) + web portal (www.asiatech.ir deadline exceeded) both down — ISP-specific isolation likely under CRA directive or sustained infrastructure degradation; notably 5/47 Asiatech IP ranges (10.6%) remain externally reachable, suggesting NIN-hosted domestic services still respond",
      "Snapp (snapp.ir) remains in redirect-loop error state (stopped after 10 redirects) — unchanged across all observed passes; persistent DPI rule-state fluctuation or application-layer misconfiguration on NIN-routed traffic",
      "Shaparak payment gateway (www.shaparak.ir) deadline-exceeded timeout persists — domestic payment infrastructure degradation or targeted application-layer filtering at NIN layer",
      "Saman Bank (sb24.ir) latency improved significantly to 3,117ms from 4,260ms — breaks the upward oscillation trend (3,197 → 3,615 → 3,340 → 4,260 → 3,117ms); suggests transient NIN congestion relief but variance remains high",
      "Foreign platforms (Google, Telegram, Instagram, YouTube, WhatsApp, Wikipedia, GitHub, Cloudflare) all reachable from outside with low latency (58-428ms) — confirms filtering is directional (inbound to Iran blocked, outbound from Iran allowed) not BGP withdrawal",
      "Circumvention infrastructure (Tor Project, BridgeDB, Snowflake broker, Psiphon) all externally reachable — endpoints not themselves blocked, but protocol-level filtering at TIC gateways prevents Iranian users from establishing Tor/VPN tunnels regardless of endpoint availability"
    ],
    "affected_services": [
      "TIC gateways (2.187.1.1 connection refused, 78.38.112.1 timeout)",
      "Irancell gateway (5.232.0.1 timeout — reverted from connection refused, behavioral oscillation)",
      "Asiatech gateway (94.182.0.1 timeout) + web portal (www.asiatech.ir deadline exceeded)",
      "Electro DNS (78.157.42.100 timeout)",
      "Snapp (snapp.ir redirect loop, 10 redirects)",
      "Shaparak payment gateway (www.shaparak.ir timeout)",
      "Saman Bank (sb24.ir — 3,117ms latency, improved from 4,260ms but still elevated)"
    ],
    "public_summary": "Iran remains in sustained stealth blackout posture: all four major ISP international gateways externally unreachable while BGP routes hold and domestic services function normally. Irancell gateway behavior oscillated — reverted from active TCP RST back to silent timeout, indicating ongoing DPI appliance tuning rather than stable policy. Notable improvement: Saman Bank latency dropped from 4,260ms to 3,117ms, suggesting transient NIN congestion relief. The protocol whitelist continues to allow only ~4.3% of IP ranges (46/1068) to respond externally.",
    "insight": "The Irancell gateway oscillation (timeout → RST → timeout) across three consecutive observation passes reveals that Iran's filtering infrastructure is actively being reconfigured — operators are tuning DPI appliance behavior in real time, and the system has not reached the steady-state maturity suggested by the prior pass's apparent convergence.",
    "recommendation": "Monitor Irancell gateway (5.232.0.1) on the next 2-3 passes to determine if the oscillation settles into a stable mode — this is a rare observable signal of active DPI reconfiguration. Continue tracking Saman Bank latency as a leading indicator of NIN congestion dynamics; the 3,117ms reading breaks the upward trend but the wide variance (3,197-4,260ms range) suggests non-stationary congestion requiring continued observation."
